# CYS-ACR-mod2-alkene — alternative mod2 for the acrylamide pre-Michael input case
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the C=C still drawn (the free drug
# SMILES form, e.g. ibrutinib's CH2=CHC(=O)N-pyrazolopyrimidine or
# osimertinib's N-methylacrylamide), this mod2 block REPLACES the default
# `data_mod_CYS-ACR-mod2` in CYS-ACR.cif. It encodes the Michael-addition
# chemistry that the bond declaration triggers:
#
#   (1) Change Cα=Cβ from double to single bond
#   (2) Add H on Cα (Michael addition transfers one proton to the alpha carbon
#       from solvent/active-site water)
#   (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp2 (CR1) to sp3 (CT)
#   (4) The new SG–Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched either:
#   CYS-ACR-pre          (internal acrylamide, R-CH=CH-C(=O)-N)
#   CYS-ACR-pre-terminal (terminal acrylamide, CH2=CH-C(=O)-N, Ibrutinib-class)
#
# For the terminal-acrylamide case (R = H on Cβ, no Cγ substituent on the
# warhead), the JS detector additionally appends one extra _chem_link_angle
# row to the link block to constrain the second H on Cβ:
#   1 SG 2 <CB> 2 <HCB-new> 109.5 3.0
# (Cβ's two H's plus SG and Cα fill its sp3 valence with standard tetrahedral
# angles around the new thioether.)
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime (same set as CYS-ACR.cif):
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id   (e.g. C13 in osimertinib's acryl)
#   <CA>  ← Cα atom-id
#   <HCA> ← H to add on Cα (the Michael-addition proton; named to follow the
#            ligand's existing H-naming convention)
#
# Chemistry note: the post-Michael Cα-Cβ bond is sp3-sp3 single, ~1.54 Å.
# The new H on Cα fills the sp3 valence that the double bond no longer occupies.
# Both carbons retype from CR1 (sp2 vinyl) to CT (sp3 tetrahedral aliphatic).
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md Appendix A.2 (acrylamide mechanism)
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf §3.1 (chem_mod semantics)

data_mod_CYS-ACR-mod2

# (1) Change Cα=Cβ from double → single
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-ACR-mod2 change <CB> <CA> single 1.54 0.02

# (2) Add a new H on Cα (the Michael-addition proton)
# (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp2 (CR1) → sp3 (CT)
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-ACR-mod2 add    <HCA> <HCA> H HCH1 .
 CYS-ACR-mod2 change <CA>  .     C CT   .
 CYS-ACR-mod2 change <CB>  .     C CT   .
